  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "No, we won't be talking the next day \n\nI ain't got nothin' to say (Hell nah) \n\nI ain't lookin' for my one true love \n\nYeah, that ship sailed away\n\nShivansh and Tina are playing a game. The players move in alternating turns with Shivansh starting first.\n\nThey have integers NNN and KKK. In one move, a player has to:\n\n\nChoose any non-negative integer XXX such that KX≤NK^X \\le NKX≤N;\nSubtract KXK^XKX from NNN.\nThe player who cannot make a move loses. If both players play optimally, find the winner of the game.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — as mentioned in the statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line `Shivansh` if Shivansh wins the game, otherwise `Tina`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `Tina`, `TINA`, `tina`, and `TiNa` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^{5}1≤T≤105",
      "0≤N≤1090 \\leq N \\leq 10^{9}0≤N≤109",
      "2≤K≤1092 \\leq K \\leq 10^{9}2≤K≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 2\n4 3\n0 10000",
        "output": "Shivansh\nTina\nTina",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nShivansh chooses X=1X = 1X=1 and subtracts 212^{1}21 from 222 to get 000.\n\nSince Tina cannot make a move now, Shivansh wins.\nTest case 222:\n\nShivansh chooses X=1X = 1X=1 and subtracts 313^{1}31 from 444 to get 111.\nTina chooses X=0X = 0X=0 and subtracts 303^{0}30 from 111 to get 000.\n\nSince Shivansh cannot make a move now, Tina wins.\nTest case 333: Shivansh cannot reduce the number further, it is already 000, so he loses."
      }
    ]
  },
